abstract: >-
  A candidate formal statement, in Lean 4 with Mathlib, of the Clay Millennium problem
  "Yang–Mills existence and mass gap" and an existence-only variant; machine-checked sanity and
  non-vacuity results; an adversarial-review methodology and its findings; a research library
  compiled and cross-checked by AI agents; and a research programme for an independent proof. This work does NOT prove existence
  or a mass gap. Its main design elements also appear in the earlier candidate statement of
  K. Rémondière (Zenodo, 10.5281/zenodo.23650415). AI systems (Anthropic's Claude via Claude Code) carried out most of the work; see
  the AI-use disclosure in the paper (paper/main.pdf, Section 9). Licensing is by file type
  (Lean code and scripts: Apache-2.0; all other content: CC BY 4.0; see LICENSE).
